# Auth and RBAC

## Patterns
- HTTP JWT strategy: RS256, bearer or `access_token` cookie (`libs/auth-lib`)
- Guards compose at gateway: JWT → roles → permissions → maintenance
- Permission map: `libs/auth-lib/src/permissions/default-permissions.config.ts`
- Sessions persist refresh JTIs; logout/refresh rotation deletes old session

## Rules
- New protected routes need explicit `@Roles` / `@Permissions` (or documented public intent)
- Admin impersonation must be audited and time-bounded
- Password reset / email verify / 2FA flows must invalidate or rotate sessions appropriately
- Validate token `iss` / `aud` / `type` when touching token verification
- WS handshake must use the shared WS auth util — do not invent a weaker path
- Do not store recoverable plaintext passwords or long-lived secrets in Redis without TTL + purpose scoping
